    "isDuplicateOf": null,
    "content": "Feedzai's Dan Holmes discussed the Financial Conduct Authority's halved stablecoin capital charge. He warned that traditional financial institutions attempting to run cryptocurrency operations on a separate, isolated technology stack will ultimately fail to scale and will end up carrying the underlying risks. Banks must integrate digital assets properly rather than treating them as a secondary side project.",
